  "glossTavolaText": "A recipe in the Recipe Book, like the illustrated plates of herbaria: \"1 Plate of 3\". On a plant's Page the Plates you don't have are empty slots with the grade circle.",
  "glossLaboratorioTerm": "Laboratory",
  "glossLaboratorioText": "Your base, the greenhouse shed at the edge of the woods: you work inside it, with the Recipe Book, Pantry and Shelf.",
  "glossRicettarioTerm": "Recipe Book",
  "glossRicettarioText": "The collection of Plates, one per country: a Page for each plant and, at the top, the Mythics of the Area, numbered.",
  "glossComponenteTerm": "Component",
  "glossComponenteText": "A piece of the name of an incomplete Plate (\"Frosted Eranthis Tincture of…\"): Uncommons, Rares and Mythics come out of the Trove of Experience with components still to find.",
  "glossRiciclatoTerm": "Recycled",
  "glossRiciclatoText": "A duplicate from the Trove of Experience: 3 recycled of a grade make a component of the same grade, 9 one of the grade above, for a little Vis.",
  "glossDispensaTerm": "Pantry",
  "glossDispensaText": "The Essences you've drawn, each with its traits, purity (from the plant's study level when you drew it) and its Vis.",
  "glossPozioneTerm": "Potion",
  "glossPozioneText": "Brewed from a recipe with the Vis of your Essences. It has a potency from 1 to 10, mostly from purity: the better you know the plants, the stronger it is. You keep it on the Shelf or use it.",
  "glossToccoTerm": "Touch",
  "glossToccoText": "The adjective the plant in the free slot gives the potion (Lush, Clear, Prescient, Bountiful): when you use it, it adds a small effect.",
  "glossPozioneGuastataTerm": "Spoiled potion",
  "glossPozioneGuastataText": "A drinkable potion with a toxic plant in the free slot: the Vis are lost, but you learn the plant is toxic.",
  "glossScaffaleTerm": "Shelf",
  "glossScaffaleText": "The potions you have: keep them for the collection or use them. The effect lasts 7 days, as strong as the potency.",
  "legendPotions": "Potions",
  "legendVessel": "The vessel shows the recipe's base (Infusion, Tincture, Philtre…), the colour of the liquid its traits: one layer per trait. The icon at the top right is the effect.",
  "viewMet": "Met",
  "erbarioSpecies": "Species",
  "tipOfDayTitle": "Tip of the day",
  "tip01": "The more you study a plant, the purer the Essences you draw from it: purity goes from 40% (a plant you never studied) to 100% (a plant you have Mastery of).",
  "tip02": "A potion's Potency depends mostly on the purity of the Essences you use: the better you know the plants in a recipe, the stronger your potions.",
  "tip03": "The Common Plates of the Recipe Book are learned by studying: when you pass level 1 of a species, that plant's Common Plate enters your Recipe Book.",
  "tip04": "Uncommon, Rare and Mythic Plates come out of the Trove of Experience incomplete, with their name in pieces: each missing piece is a Component, found by opening more Trove of Experience.",
  "tip05": "Mythic Plates are only found by opening a mythic-grade Trove of Experience.",
  "tip06": "If the Trove of Experience gives you a Plate or a Component you already have, it's a duplicate: recycle it with a little Vis. 3 Recycled make a Component of the same grade, 9 a Component of the grade above.",
  "tip07": "Recycling a duplicate costs a little Vis, taken from your Essences: the least precious Essences are used first, so the ones with Traits stay for recipes.",
  "tip08": "Every recipe has a free slot, “any species”: the plant you put there gives the potion its Touch (Lush, Clear, Prescient or Bountiful).",
  "tip09": "Beware of the free slot in recipes to drink: with a toxic plant the potion spoils and you lose the Vis used, but you learn that plant is toxic.",
  "tip10": "In the Recipe Book, the \"Show only ready to brew\" filter keeps the Plates you can brew now; open the others to see which Essences you are missing: it's the list of plants to look for on your next outing.",
  "tip11": "When you use a potion from the Shelf, its effect lasts 7 days and is as strong as its Potency.",
  "tip12": "An Essence's Traits tell the conditions you drew it in (weather, time of day, moon); a recipe's name says which Traits it needs: “Full-moon” asks for an Essence drawn under the Full moon.",
  "tip13": "The XP you earn studying a species stays to Cash in until you draw the first Essence of that species: only then does it become real XP.",
  "tip14": "The meaning of symbols, colours and grades is in the Legend: Settings → Legend and glossary.",
  "tip15": "In the game a plant is never picked: you photograph it and draw its Vis. Plants stay where they are, untouched.",
